  "readmeFile": "NuGet.README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.1.3 (2026-11-12): the linq2db adapter now executes on SharpCoreDB instead of SQLite, so a password is honoured and rows live in an encrypted SharpCoreDB file, and the SQL shapes that blocked it are fixed - pretty-printed INSERTs, SELECT-list projection, bare and negated boolean WHERE, LIKE with ESCAPE, scalar EXISTS, and hex byte[]/Guid literals. Previous: v2.1.2 (2026-10-26): patch release with no API changes - a bound text parameter is no longer re-scanned as SQL text, so a value holding an apostrophe, a doubled quote, a backslash, a comma or a parenthesis now round-trips exactly instead of landing in the neighbouring column or failing with \"Mismatched parentheses in VALUES clause\"; full detail in docs/CHANGELOG.md. Previous: v2.1.1 (2026-10-25): patch release with no API changes. A float[] parameter now reaches a VECTOR(n) column as a vector instead of the literal text \"System.Single[]\", and ORDER BY vec_distance_*() LIMIT k now reaches the vector index instead of a full scan. Previous: v2.1.0 (2026-10-10): .NET 11 / C# 15 preview release line — net11.0-only, native Zstandard compression (quality presets 1/5/19 + frame checksum), Runtime Async, an additive C# 15 API surface (SharpCoreDB.Net11), and the Munarium-inspired DiskANN index + content-verified index artifacts. The net10.0 / C# 14 line is the v2.0 stable packages, now parked on release/v2.0. See docs/net11/UPGRADE.md for details.",
